#  ✔ STATUS 2026-09-17: RAN GREEN on its FIRST execution, with every pinned witness present and every
#  RED path fired. Witnesses were derived independently (a separate python re-implementation of κ/NORMK
#  and the relevant census) BEFORE the gate section was written, never captured from this module's own
#  output — which is why the first run matched. Gated in gate_registers.sh.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  phonometa.la — THE METACURSIVE PHONOSEMANTIC-TOPOLOGY LEVEL
#
#  THE GAP (LA_TOMORROW.md, Erik 2026-09-15): "The METACURSIVE phonosemantic-topology level
#  (transspecies speakability). psc.la/phonsem.la are THE BASE; the metacursive layer that makes the
#  phonosemantic topology speakable transspecies is not its own gate. The transspecies FUNCTOR is
#  Category 3 (external, needs another channel); the metacursive phonosemantic LEVEL itself is
#  Category-1-buildable."  This builds the LEVEL. It does NOT build the functor and does not claim it.
#
#  ★ WHAT "METACURSIVE" MEANS HERE, CONCRETELY. The base level (psc.la, GENERATED by specpipe.la — read,
#  never edited) gives each phonym an INVARIANT Θ_P = its distinct formant peaks, and composes two
#  phonyms by SUPERPOSING their spectra: SYN_INV(a)(b) = Θ_P(a ⧺ b). The METACURSIVE level is that
#  topology applied to ITS OWN OUTPUTS — invariants composed with invariants — and the question is
#  whether the level is CLOSED under itself and comes to a STAND. Four things are asserted, and each can fail:
#      (1) Θ_P is TWO-SIDED: it REMOVES (6 raw peaks → 3) **and** it is IDEMPOTENT.
#      (2) the level is CLOSED and ORDER-FREE one step up: composing invariants associates,
#          SYN_INV(SYN_INV(a)(b))(c) = SYN_INV(a)(SYN_INV(b)(c)), 9 peaks either way.
#      (3) the METACURSIVE FIXED POINT: an invariant superposed with ITSELF returns itself,
#          SYN_INV(a)(a) = Θ_P(a). This is where the level comes to a stand.
#      (4) the CONSTITUENT LAW SURVIVES the meta step: the double compound still preserves each parent's
#          invariants, and still REFUSES psc.la's own declared non-constituent control (Depth's /ɔ/).
#
#  ★ (1) IS TWO-SIDED ON PURPOSE, and it is the lesson this stack keeps re-learning. Idempotence ALONE is
#  satisfied by the IDENTITY function — Θ_P(Θ_P(x)) = Θ_P(x) holds trivially if Θ_P does nothing at all.
#  So "it comes to a stand" is only a law when paired with "it MOVED first". Same shape as autocompress.la's
#  Δ_ν. A one-sided version of (1) or (3) would pass with the whole module gutted.
#
#  ★★ A FINDING ABOUT THE BASE MODULE, stated precisely because precision is the whole point here.
#  psc.la declares `PMODE_REC : the mode is RECOVERABLE from the phonetic invariant`. As written it is
#      PMODE_REC(a)(b) = IF(str_eq(PINV("⊗")(a)(b))(PINV("⊕")(a)(b)))(FALSE)(TRUE)
#  and `PINV(sym)(a)(b) = sym ⧺ ":" ⧺ LREN(SYN_INV(a)(b))` — where SYN_INV DOES NOT DEPEND ON sym. The two
#  strings therefore differ in their FIRST CHARACTER and nowhere else, so PMODE_REC returns TRUE for every
#  input. It compares the LABEL it just prepended, not the phonetics. Strip the label and the two modes
#  give a byte-identical invariant, because psc.la defines exactly ONE composition law (superposition).
#  **So the mode is NOT recoverable from the phonetic invariant alone, and this module gates that NEGATIVE.**
#  ★ SAID FAIRLY, because the distinction matters: this is **NOT a false green**. build.sh's psc block
#  (:1566–:1582) asserts W1–W6 — preservation, the render, duration, idempotence — and **never asserts
#  PMODE_REC at all.** It is an exported definition whose comment claims more than the code can show,
#  not a gate that is passing when it should fail. And psc.la is GENERATED from `psc_spec.la:50`, so the
#  line to change is the SPEC's, never this file's. Nothing here edits either. [[generated modules]]
#
#  ★ SCOPE, so the title is not over-read [B]: this gates the metacursive LEVEL — the phonosemantic
#  topology closed under its own outputs and standing. **TRANSSPECIES SPEAKABILITY IS NOT BUILT AND NOT
#  CLAIMED.** The functor between two species' realisations needs a SECOND CHANNEL the system does not
#  have; LA_TOMORROW files it Category 3, external, and it stays there. What a closed, standing topology
#  buys is the PRECONDITION for such a functor, not the functor.
#
#  GATE (gate_registers.sh §40 — ran green 2026-09-17, REGS_DRAFT guard removed; SECD VM leg not yet run)
#        the four assertions above, the negative mode-recovery finding, and — as a check on THIS module's
#        reading of its dependency — a recomputation of build.sh's own pinned psc witness.
#        RED PATHS: (1) LDEDUP made the identity — Θ_P removes nothing, so the "it moved" half of (1) and
#        the fixed point (3) both go F, while a one-sided law would still have read green; (2) LSUB made
#        constant-true — the non-constituent control reads as PRESERVED and (4) stops discriminating.
#  ★ EVIDENTIAL: [W] the four assertions, the negative finding, the cross-check; [B] the scope above.
#  ⚖ RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-18 against the standing rule (FREEZE-TRACKF.md F35): of this module's 6 pinned witnesses — red-proven 3 · exact & cross-checked 1 · construction-true 2 [A: witnesses its constructor, not the claim — constituents ⊆ their union; union is associative] · cannot-fail 1 [UNWITNESSED — F28 (PM_MODE_BARE compares X with X)]. A [W] above holds ONLY where its witness is red-proven, fixture-backed or derived; each gate line's `#@ turns-red:` says which.
#  Pure integers + Scott lists ⇒ byte-identical on the C host and the SECD VM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import("psc.la")   # GENERATED by specpipe.la — READ, never edited: Z TRUE FALSE AND IF LNIL LCONS LMEM LSUB LAPP LDEDUP LREN THETA_P SYN_INV PINV PRESERVES SYN_DUR LOVE_F REC_F DEPTH_F

export PM_META PM_STAND PM_CLOSED PM_MODE_BARE

# ★ LOCAL ALIASES, and the reason is a fact about the host worth recording: tiny_host's
#   lookup_glyph returns the FIRST definition of a name (tiny_host.c:344-348), and an import’s glyphs
#   are entered BEFORE the importing file’s own. **A later `glyph THETA_P = …` therefore does NOT shadow
#   the imported one.** A mutant that tried to redefine an imported glyph would change nothing and the RED
#   path would silently never fire — a mutant that does not mutate is the vacuous gate one level up. So
#   every psc.la function this module ASSERTS about is routed through a local alias, which a mutant can reach.
glyph PM_THETA = THETA_P
glyph PM_SUB   = PRESERVES
glyph PM_SYN   = la a. la b. PM_THETA(LAPP(a)(b))
glyph PM_NOT = la b. b(FALSE)(TRUE)
glyph PM_BSTR = la b. b("T")("F")
glyph PM_LEN = Z(la self. la l. l(0)(la h. la t. add(1)(self(t))))
glyph PM_EQ = la a. la b. str_eq(LREN(a))(LREN(b))
glyph PM_JOIN = Z(la self. la l. l("")(la h. la t. concat(h)(self(t))))
glyph PMNIL = la n. la c. n
glyph PMCONS = la h. la t. la n. la c. c(h)(t)

# ── (1) Θ_P is TWO-SIDED: it MOVES, and then it STANDS ──
glyph PM_RAW   = LAPP(LOVE_F)(LOVE_F)
glyph PM_MOVED = PM_NOT(PM_EQ(PM_THETA(PM_RAW))(PM_RAW))
glyph PM_STAND = PM_EQ(PM_THETA(PM_THETA(PM_RAW)))(PM_THETA(PM_RAW))

# ── (2) the level is CLOSED and ORDER-FREE one step up ──
glyph PM_L = PM_SYN(PM_SYN(LOVE_F)(REC_F))(DEPTH_F)
glyph PM_R = PM_SYN(LOVE_F)(PM_SYN(REC_F)(DEPTH_F))
glyph PM_CLOSED = PM_EQ(PM_L)(PM_R)

# ── (3) the METACURSIVE FIXED POINT: an invariant superposed with itself returns itself ──
glyph PM_META = PM_EQ(PM_SYN(LOVE_F)(LOVE_F))(PM_THETA(LOVE_F))

# ── (4) the constituent law SURVIVES the meta step; psc.la's own non-constituent control still refused ──
glyph PM_C2 = PM_L
glyph PM_K1 = PM_SUB(LOVE_F)(PM_C2)
glyph PM_K2 = PM_SUB(REC_F)(PM_C2)
glyph PM_K3 = PM_SUB(DEPTH_F)(PM_SYN(LOVE_F)(REC_F))

# ── THE FINDING: the mode is NOT recoverable from the invariant ALONE ──
glyph PM_MODE_LABEL = PM_NOT(str_eq(PINV("⊗")(LOVE_F)(REC_F))(PINV("⊕")(LOVE_F)(REC_F)))
glyph PM_MODE_BARE  = PM_NOT(str_eq(LREN(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F)))(LREN(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F))))

# ── CROSS-CHECK: recompute build.sh's own pinned psc witness (build.sh:1583) ──
glyph PM_W = PM_JOIN(
  PMCONS(PRESERVES(LOVE_F)(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F))("L")("x"))(
  PMCONS(PRESERVES(REC_F)(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F))("R")("x"))(
  PMCONS(PRESERVES(DEPTH_F)(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F))("x")("d"))(
  PMCONS("|")(
  PMCONS(LREN(SYN_INV(LOVE_F)(REC_F)))(
  PMCONS("|")(
  PMCONS(concat("dur=")(int_to_str(SYN_DUR(6560)(6720))))(
  PMCONS("|")(
  PMCONS(str_eq(LREN(THETA_P(THETA_P(LAPP(LOVE_F)(REC_F)))))(LREN(THETA_P(LAPP(LOVE_F)(REC_F))))("i")("x"))(
  PMNIL))))))))))

glyph REPORT =
  PM_JOIN(
  PMCONS("PHONOMETA (1) Θ_P two-sided: raw peaks=")(
  PMCONS(int_to_str(PM_LEN(PM_RAW)))(
  PMCONS(" → Θ_P peaks=")(
  PMCONS(int_to_str(PM_LEN(PM_THETA(PM_RAW))))(
  PMCONS(" it MOVED:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_MOVED))(
  PMCONS(" and then STANDS (idempotent):")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_STAND))(
  PMCONS(" (idempotence alone is satisfied by the identity — both halves or neither)")(
  PMCONS("\nPHONOMETA (2) the level is CLOSED one step up: SYN_INV(SYN_INV(a)(b))(c) = SYN_INV(a)(SYN_INV(b)(c)):")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_CLOSED))(
  PMCONS(" peaks=")(
  PMCONS(int_to_str(PM_LEN(PM_L)))(
  PMCONS(" | (3) METACURSIVE FIXED POINT SYN_INV(a)(a)=Θ_P(a):")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_META))(
  PMCONS(" | (4) constituent law survives: LOVE⊆:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_K1))(
  PMCONS(" REC⊆:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_K2))(
  PMCONS(" non-constituent DEPTH⊆:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_K3))(
  PMCONS(" (must be F — psc.la's own control)")(
  PMCONS("\nPHONOMETA ★ the mode is NOT recoverable from the phonetic invariant ALONE: with psc.la's prepended label the strings differ:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_MODE_LABEL))(
  PMCONS(" but bare invariants differ:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(PM_MODE_BARE))(
  PMCONS(" — psc.la's PMODE_REC compares the LABEL it just wrote, so it is TRUE for every input. NOT a false green: build.sh's psc block asserts W1-W6 and never asserts PMODE_REC. The line to change is psc_spec.la:50, the SPEC — psc.la is GENERATED and is not edited here")(
  PMCONS("\nPHONOMETA cross-check of this module's reading of psc.la against build.sh:1583's pinned witness: ")(
  PMCONS(PM_W)(
  PMCONS(" matches:")(
  PMCONS(PM_BSTR(str_eq(PM_W)("LRd|300,870,2240,270,2300,3000,|dur=6720|i")))(
  PMCONS(" | [B] this gates the metacursive LEVEL. TRANSSPECIES SPEAKABILITY IS NOT BUILT AND NOT CLAIMED — the functor needs a second channel the system does not have (Category 3, external)")(
  PMNIL)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
glyph MAIN = print(REPORT)
